#!/bin/sh
# Rename the active Hyprland workspace. Bound to SUPER+COMMA (mirrors tmux's
# prefix+, for windows). "gaming" is refused: the persistent rule and the
# gamingWindows routing in hyprland.lua match that workspace by name.
set -eu

ws_json=$(hyprctl -j activeworkspace)
ws_id=$(printf '%s' "$ws_json" | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)["id"])')
ws_name=$(printf '%s' "$ws_json" | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)["name"])')

if [ "$ws_name" = "gaming" ]; then
    zenity --error --title 'Rename workspace' \
        --text '"gaming" is matched by name in hyprland.lua (persistent rule + gaming window routing). Renaming it would break both.' \
        2>/dev/null || true
    exit 0
fi

name=$(zenity --entry --title 'Rename workspace' \
    --text "New name for workspace \"${ws_name}\":" \
    --entry-text "$ws_name" 2>/dev/null) || exit 0
[ -n "$name" ] || exit 0

# ' and \ would break out of the Lua string in the dispatch below
case "$name" in
    *\'* | *\\* )
        zenity --error --title 'Rename workspace' \
            --text 'Single quotes and backslashes are not allowed in names.' \
            2>/dev/null || true
        exit 0
        ;;
esac

hyprctl dispatch "hl.dsp.workspace.rename({ workspace = $ws_id, name = '$name' })"
